-- Zero-shot cosplay-photo score: similarity of image_vec to a cosplay prototype minus the closer of
-- two negative prototypes (illustration, ordinary photo). Prototypes are means of jina-clip-v2
-- (truncate_dim=1024, prompt "retrieval.query") text embeddings of these phrases:
--   cosplay:      a photo of a cosplayer wearing an anime costume and wig; cosplay photography of a real person dressed as an anime character; cosplay
--   illustration: an anime illustration; a digital drawing of an anime girl
--   photo:        a regular photo of people; a screenshot or meme; a photo of food, animals or objects
-- `<#>` is the negative inner product, so this equals img·cosplay - max(img·illustration, img·photo).
-- Scores above ~0.02 are cosplay photos (precision 0.97, recall 0.88 on a hand-labelled sample).
-- STORED generated: Postgres fills existing rows on ALTER and recomputes whenever image_vec changes.

